 |year=1998 | page=56 | isbn=0-691-02565-7
 | url=https://books.google.com/books?id=arYYRoYjKacC&pg=PA174 }}</ref> so, at a distance of 3.212&nbsp;parsecs, the Sun would have an apparent magnitude:
<math>\begin{smallmatrix} m = M_v + 5\cdot\log_{10} (3.212/10) + A_V = 2.36 \end{smallmatrix}</math>,<ref>{{citation
 | display-authors=1
